      "hints": [
        "Multiply across by $(\\tan\\theta - 2\\sin\\theta)$ to get $\\tan\\theta + 2\\sin\\theta = 3\\tan\\theta - 6\\sin\\theta$.",
        "Rearrange to $2\\tan\\theta - 8\\sin\\theta = 0$ and substitute $\\tan\\theta = \\frac{\\sin\\theta}{\\cos\\theta}$.",
        "Factorise $2\\sin\\theta(1 - 4\\cos\\theta) = 0$ and solve for $\\theta$ in $0^\\circ < \\theta < 180^\\circ$."
      ],
      "walkthrough": [
        "Clear the algebraic fraction by multiplying across by the denominator:\n$$\\tan\\theta + 2\\sin\\theta = 3(\\tan\\theta - 2\\sin\\theta) = 3\\tan\\theta - 6\\sin\\theta$$",
        "Collect like trigonometric terms:\n$$2\\tan\\theta - 8\\sin\\theta = 0$$",
        "Express $\\tan\\theta$ as $\\frac{\\sin\\theta}{\\cos\\theta}$ and clear denominators:\n$$2\\left(\\frac{\\sin\\theta}{\\cos\\theta}\\right) - 8\\sin\\theta = 0 \\implies 2\\sin\\theta - 8\\sin\\theta\\cos\\theta = 0$$\n$$2\\sin\\theta(1 - 4\\cos\\theta) = 0$$",
        "Solve for the valid root in the open interval $0^\\circ < \\theta < 180^\\circ$ (where $\\sin\\theta \\ne 0$):\n$$1 - 4\\cos\\theta = 0 \\implies \\cos\\theta = \\frac{1}{4} = 0.25$$\n$$\\theta = \\cos^{-1}(0.25) \\approx 75.5^\\circ$$"
      ],
      "checking": {
